## 5. AI Techniques

### Natural Language Processing

Resume text and job descriptions are cleaned and normalized before analysis.

### TF-IDF Vectorization

TF-IDF converts text into numerical features based on the importance of words within the documents.

### Cosine Similarity

Cosine similarity compares the resulting vectors to estimate how similar the resume and job description are.

The resulting similarity score represents textual similarity. It is not a probability of being hired or a validated measure of professional suitability.

### Skill Extraction

A configurable skill dictionary identifies skills mentioned in resume text and job requirements.

### Skill Gap Analysis

The application compares extracted resume skills with the skills required by a job description to identify potential gaps.

### Recommendation Logic

Career recommendations are ranked using defined matching criteria, such as relevant skills and text similarity.

These techniques provide meaningful AI processing without requiring a paid LLM API.

